  "summary": "Backus's function-level language from his 1977 Turing Award lecture: programs are built from primitive functions and combining forms without variables, with an algebra of programs. FL (IBM Almaden, 1980s) was its successor with exceptions, I/O and higher-order functions.",
  "status": "historical",
  "defined_by": [
    "academic-paper"
  ],
  "influenced_by": [
    "apl"
  ],
  "level_notes": {
    "0": "No original IBM FP/FL implementation source is public; level 0 lists third-party FP interpreters and compilers (Valencia, Biagioni). The Berkeley FP manual and the IFP Byte article are listed at level 2.",
    "1": "Defined by Backus's 1978 paper and the IBM FL language manuals (scanned at the Software Preservation Group)."
  },
